  <Docs>
    <summary>
            An <see cref="T:System.Net.IPEndPoint" /> that opts an endpoint into the DirectTls transport. Bind it with
            <c>KestrelServerOptions.Listen(...)</c> (or <c>ListenAnyIP</c>/<c>ListenLocalhost</c>) to serve that
            endpoint over the native, file-descriptor-bound OpenSSL TLS session instead of <c>SslStream</c>.
            </summary>
    <remarks>
      <para>
            DirectTls is TLS-only. The endpoint's <see cref="P:Microsoft.AspNetCore.Server.Kestrel.Transport.DirectTls.DirectTlsEndpoint.Options" /> must supply a server certificate (via
            <see cref="P:Microsoft.AspNetCore.Server.Kestrel.Transport.DirectTls.DirectTlsEndpointOptions.ServerCertificate" /> or
            <see cref="P:Microsoft.AspNetCore.Server.Kestrel.Transport.DirectTls.DirectTlsEndpointOptions.ServerCertificateSelector" />).
            </para>
    </remarks>
  </Docs>
